(998194, 118341, 10432, '<td valign="top">Very cute - nice lighting, great expression on the baby.  Would have liked to have seen a closer connection between the baby and the bear.  Not sure I like the cotton balls (?) piled up.  Good luck!</td>', 'Very cute - nice lighting, great expression on the baby.  Would have liked to have seen a closer connection between the baby and the bear.  Not sure I like the cotton balls (?) piled up.  Good luck!', '2004-11-08 01:12:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(998201, 119520, 10432, '<td valign="top">Very pretty flower.  Lighting seems a bit harsh for this subject.   Too many shadows.</td>', 'Very pretty flower.  Lighting seems a bit harsh for this subject.   Too many shadows.', '2004-11-08 01:15:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(998213, 119554, 10432, '<td valign="top">Photo tilted to the left and subject does not hold much interest.  Horizon cuts photo in half.</td>', 'Photo tilted to the left and subject does not hold much interest.  Horizon cuts photo in half.', '2004-11-08 01:21:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(998269, 118370, 22781, '<td valign="top">Winner!</td>', 'Winner!', '2004-11-08 02:44:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(998273, 118387, 25571, '<td valign="top">Colours are very nice and rich. Also really enjoy the crop, although i think i would''ve prefered it without the tree on the far right. Also, I would recommend bringing the ''orange'' frame line a lot closer to the picture. The separation, as much as being unbalanced (bigger black spacing inside then outside) creates a void between the picture itself and ''end'' of the pic. See my ''October free Study'' picture "Heaven-Seen-Through-Urban-Eyes" to better see/understand what i mean (I am in no way implying that my picture is better then yours).</td>', 'Colours are very nice and rich. Also really enjoy the crop, although i think i would''ve prefered it without the tree on the far right. Also, I would recommend bringing the ''orange'' frame line a lot closer to the picture. The separation, as much as being unbalanced (bigger black spacing inside then outside) creates a void between the picture itself and ''end'' of the pic. See my ''October free Study'' picture "Heaven-Seen-Through-Urban-Eyes" to better see/understand what i mean (I am in no way implying that my picture is better then yours).', '2004-11-08 02:49:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(998278, 119521, 25571, '<td valign="top">Very nice Framing of the picture. The colours are nice and warm, even for a November application. Perharps would''ve been a little nicer without the gray darmac on the far right. Perharps with a clever croping, it could be removed without loosing too much of the wall. If a chance comes, a re-shoot of this location, but from a lower perspective would give good results, perharps in catching more of the sky to create a good contrast with the red and green...</td>', 'Very nice Framing of the picture. The colours are nice and warm, even for a November application. Perharps would''ve been a little nicer without the gray darmac on the far right. Perharps with a clever croping, it could be removed without loosing too much of the wall. If a chance comes, a re-shoot of this location, but from a lower perspective would give good results, perharps in catching more of the sky to create a good contrast with the red and green...', '2004-11-08 02:52:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(998280, 118954, 25571, '<td valign="top">Amazing Contrast in colours. Perfect representation of November. The grading of colours from Rich to sad-gray is very well done. For some reason, i wish i could''ve seen a little more on the left, perharps a ''wide'' angle shot would''ve helped. This place is pure delight for an ''Halloween'' or ''creepy'' Tim Burton feature film (Sleepy Hollow-esque). I would really like to know where it was taken!</td>', 'Amazing Contrast in colours. Perfect representation of November. The grading of colours from Rich to sad-gray is very well done. For some reason, i wish i could''ve seen a little more on the left, perharps a ''wide'' angle shot would''ve helped. This place is pure delight for an ''Halloween'' or ''creepy'' Tim Burton feature film (Sleepy Hollow-esque). I would really like to know where it was taken!', '2004-11-08 02:54:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(998285, 119018, 25571, '<td valign="top">This picture seems very interesting and nice. Unfortunatly, because of the "very big" frame, we do not see much of it. The colours look really rich, while the sky could''ve used some work. <br/> <br/>As a recommendation, i would propose to remove the frame completly, and just add a little framing line, a few pixel-distance from the actual picture (black background) with a nice golden colour. This would bring out a lot more of the image. <br/> <br/>An unwriten rule of framing: Never use the dominant or most ''foreground'' colour as a frame display. Go with the soft and unique colours. (in your case, yellow, green or Red would''ve probably given more punch).</td>', 'This picture seems very interesting and nice. Unfortunatly, because of the "very big" frame, we do not see much of it. The colours look really rich, while the sky could''ve used some work.  As a recommendation, i would propose to remove the frame completly, and just add a little framing line, a few pixel-distance from the actual picture (black background) with a nice golden colour. This would bring out a lot more of the image.  An unwriten rule of framing: Never use the dominant or most ''foreground'' colour as a frame display. Go with the soft and unique colours. (in your case, yellow, green or Red would''ve probably given more punch).', '2004-11-08 02:58:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(998297, 119526, 28962, '<td valign="top">The sand in front isn''t that interesting. A bit closer to the dunes would improve the composition imho.</td>', 'The sand in front isn''t that interesting. A bit closer to the dunes would improve the composition imho.', '2004-11-08 03:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(998302, 119078, 28070, '<td valign="top">Pretty cool migration.  I wish it was somewhat closer though.  not much filling the space.</td>', 'Pretty cool migration.  I wish it was somewhat closer though.  not much filling the space.', '2004-11-08 03:32:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(998311, 118525, 28097, '<td valign="top">woulda been much better without the frame</td>', 'woulda been much better without the frame', '2004-11-08 03:44:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(998314, 119286, 23478, '<td valign="top">Great color contrast.</td>', 'Great color contrast.', '2004-11-08 03:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(998317, 119399, 23478, '<td valign="top">Excellent colors and perspective.</td>', 'Excellent colors and perspective.', '2004-11-08 03:53:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(998321, 118778, 23478, '<td valign="top">Interesting reflections, they create a certain illusion.</td>', 'Interesting reflections, they create a certain illusion.', '2004-11-08 03:54:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(998323, 119340, 23478, '<td valign="top">great silouette.</td>', 'great silouette.', '2004-11-08 03:57:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(998324, 119520, 24459, '<td valign="top">If I could advise something, I would recommend to put the flower horizontal, or at least away from the background. Because it''s so close this pic is spoiled by unnecessary shadows made by flash.<br/>Also using an external source of light would help. Sory if I''m wrong, but I think you used flash and that makes the pic flat. <br/>Still a nice composition.</td>', 'If I could advise something, I would recommend to put the flower horizontal, or at least away from the background. Because it''s so close this pic is spoiled by unnecessary shadows made by flash.Also using an external source of light would help. Sory if I''m wrong, but I think you used flash and that makes the pic flat. Still a nice composition.', '2004-11-08 03:57:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(998326, 118987, 23478, '<td valign="top">Great capture of the water''s motion.</td>', 'Great capture of the water''s motion.', '2004-11-08 03:59:27.000000', NULL, 1),
