(1012868, 118963, 7869, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by alisasaur:</b></div><hr/><i> The fact that this photo received so many ones shows that people automatically vote a photo down simply because George W. Bush is in the shot.  This is an amazing photograph.  The photo is great; the focus is perfect.  I''m not assuming that you are a conservative, but I am, and I know that I wouldn''t vote a photo down just because John Kerry is in it.  People are seriously pathetic. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>well, I don''t think ppl voted down because the subject. first, when you''re not American this doesn''t mean "November" in any way. This is an international web site, do you think that THIS says November for someone in India or Spain? Plus technically, the color balance IS pathetic, the picture is dark, and the background distracting. It doesn''t matter who is the main subject.</td>', 'Originally posted by alisasaur: The fact that this photo received so many ones shows that people automatically vote a photo down simply because George W. Bush is in the shot.  This is an amazing photograph.  The photo is great; the focus is perfect.  I''m not assuming that you are a conservative, but I am, and I know that I wouldn''t vote a photo down just because John Kerry is in it.  People are seriously pathetic.   well, I don''t think ppl voted down because the subject. first, when you''re not American this doesn''t mean "November" in any way. This is an international web site, do you think that THIS says November for someone in India or Spain? Plus technically, the color balance IS pathetic, the picture is dark, and the background distracting. It doesn''t matter who is the main subject.', '2004-11-15 22:42:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1012894, 119399, 29168, '<td valign="top"><b><i>Congrats!</i></b> <br/> <br/>Can you tell us, was there any type of lens filter used for this shot? Thanks.</td>', 'Congrats!  Can you tell us, was there any type of lens filter used for this shot? Thanks.', '2004-11-15 23:23:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1012931, 119399, 6008, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gruvin:</b></div><hr/><i> <b><i>Congrats!</i></b> <br/> <br/>Can you tell us, was there any type of lens filter used for this shot? Thanks. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I used a cokin G2 graduated neutral density filter.</td>', 'Originally posted by gruvin: Congrats!  Can you tell us, was there any type of lens filter used for this shot? Thanks.   I used a cokin G2 graduated neutral density filter.', '2004-11-15 23:49:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013216, 118525, 28962, '<td valign="top">First of all I would like to thank everybody for their comments. <br/> <br/>For those who have problems with borders: Usually I  keep my borders simple, a single line with some white or black depending on the content. But this is because I usually do stillifes with a modern and very minimalistic style. The simple border matches that. A Rembrand of Vermeer needs a heavy golden frame to match the tast of the period. <br/>This image tried to go back to the pen drawings from before the camera and the border had to match this. <br/> <br/>So for those who just don''t like borders because they are borders: please try to imagine why it is there and what it tries to accomplice. Just comment that it would be so much better without (as the first comment did) simply will not do!</td>', 'First of all I would like to thank everybody for their comments.  For those who have problems with borders: Usually I  keep my borders simple, a single line with some white or black depending on the content. But this is because I usually do stillifes with a modern and very minimalistic style. The simple border matches that. A Rembrand of Vermeer needs a heavy golden frame to match the tast of the period. This image tried to go back to the pen drawings from before the camera and the border had to match this.  So for those who just don''t like borders because they are borders: please try to imagine why it is there and what it tries to accomplice. Just comment that it would be so much better without (as the first comment did) simply will not do!', '2004-11-16 04:58:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013239, 119453, 22964, '<td valign="top">Its sooo cute, great eyes and good choice of background. I also own one, it seems so innocent but few people know this dog is used to hunt wild boars!!</td>', 'Its sooo cute, great eyes and good choice of background. I also own one, it seems so innocent but few people know this dog is used to hunt wild boars!!', '2004-11-16 05:37:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013258, 118963, 20364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Roboj:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by alisasaur:</b></div><hr/><i> The fact that this photo received so many ones shows that people automatically vote a photo down simply because George W. Bush is in the shot.  This is an amazing photograph.  The photo is great; the focus is perfect.  I''m not assuming that you are a conservative, but I am, and I know that I wouldn''t vote a photo down just because John Kerry is in it.  People are seriously pathetic. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>well, I don''t think ppl voted down because the subject. first, when you''re not American this doesn''t mean "November" in any way. This is an international web site, do you think that THIS says November for someone in India or Spain? Plus technically, the color balance IS pathetic, the picture is dark, and the background distracting. It doesn''t matter who is the main subject. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I am completely aware this is an international site.  And unless you bury your head in the sand you know that elections here in our great nation are held in November.<br/> <br/>Secondly, as far as my photo goes....you''re an idiot.</td>', 'Originally posted by Roboj: Originally posted by alisasaur: The fact that this photo received so many ones shows that people automatically vote a photo down simply because George W. Bush is in the shot.  This is an amazing photograph.  The photo is great; the focus is perfect.  I''m not assuming that you are a conservative, but I am, and I know that I wouldn''t vote a photo down just because John Kerry is in it.  People are seriously pathetic.   well, I don''t think ppl voted down because the subject. first, when you''re not American this doesn''t mean "November" in any way. This is an international web site, do you think that THIS says November for someone in India or Spain? Plus technically, the color balance IS pathetic, the picture is dark, and the background distracting. It doesn''t matter who is the main subject.   I am completely aware this is an international site.  And unless you bury your head in the sand you know that elections here in our great nation are held in November. Secondly, as far as my photo goes....you''re an idiot.', '2004-11-16 06:17:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013264, 118963, 20364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ajschmidt:</b></div><hr/><i> Dumb ass fool... Oh, sorry.  Could not help my self.  Your real soft on the focus.  Humm... soft focus... so true. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is a photo challenge.  Look at it from that perspective.  Dumb ass liberal...err..oh, sorry...could not help my self....</td>', 'Originally posted by ajschmidt: Dumb ass fool... Oh, sorry.  Could not help my self.  Your real soft on the focus.  Humm... soft focus... so true.   This is a photo challenge.  Look at it from that perspective.  Dumb ass liberal...err..oh, sorry...could not help my self....', '2004-11-16 06:28:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013268, 118963, 20364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Koriyama:</b></div><hr/><i> This will only work for those interested in a particular brand of politics. 1 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Once again...this is a photo challenge site (unless I am missing something), look at the photo from that point of view...That''s all I ask...</td>', 'Originally posted by Koriyama: This will only work for those interested in a particular brand of politics. 1   Once again...this is a photo challenge site (unless I am missing something), look at the photo from that point of view...That''s all I ask...', '2004-11-16 06:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013272, 118963, 20364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Blackdog:</b></div><hr/><i> Give us a break, I''m sick of seeing these shots, even in the UK, so I don''t know how you must feel over there?  OK, its focussed and he looks like he''s making a point but the background is far too distracting and a calendar?  You''re joking right? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>First, you sound very biased and by being in the UK I know that you are.  So, you admit the photo is focused and it look as though he is making a point so why not just stop there?  Why bring the politics in?  This is a photo challenge site.  Judge my photo from that perspective.</td>', 'Originally posted by Blackdog: Give us a break, I''m sick of seeing these shots, even in the UK, so I don''t know how you must feel over there?  OK, its focussed and he looks like he''s making a point but the background is far too distracting and a calendar?  You''re joking right?   First, you sound very biased and by being in the UK I know that you are.  So, you admit the photo is focused and it look as though he is making a point so why not just stop there?  Why bring the politics in?  This is a photo challenge site.  Judge my photo from that perspective.', '2004-11-16 06:33:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013279, 118963, 20364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Artyste:</b></div><hr/><i> Your color balance could use some tweaking, as I see a lot of reds in the skin tones.  The focus isn''t on your subject quite enough, and could have benefitted from a tighter crop.. (not much, but getting rid of that W in the corner would have helped a lot.  <br/>Not being American, I could also question the tie-in to the month, but luckily I know that November is the usual election month, so I wonder if you might be suffering there as well. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Agreed.  I think I had too many reds in the photo.  I will adjust before I put the print up for sale.  The "W" was the first letter of our hometown but I thought it would be cool to keep it in.  I felt it fit well with the President...</td>', 'Originally posted by Artyste: Your color balance could use some tweaking, as I see a lot of reds in the skin tones.  The focus isn''t on your subject quite enough, and could have benefitted from a tighter crop.. (not much, but getting rid of that W in the corner would have helped a lot.  Not being American, I could also question the tie-in to the month, but luckily I know that November is the usual election month, so I wonder if you might be suffering there as well.   Agreed.  I think I had too many reds in the photo.  I will adjust before I put the print up for sale.  The "W" was the first letter of our hometown but I thought it would be cool to keep it in.  I felt it fit well with the President...', '2004-11-16 06:36:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013283, 118963, 20364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by graphicfunk:</b></div><hr/><i> returning for comments:<br/>You got a conservative''s eight for the Nov. winners. lol </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re a true American!</td>', 'Originally posted by graphicfunk: returning for comments:You got a conservative''s eight for the Nov. winners. lol   You''re a true American!', '2004-11-16 06:39:53.000000', NULL, 0),
